# 🔴 NEVER COMMIT THESE. The release keystore is the app's identity: Android only
# installs an update over an existing app if it is signed with the SAME key. If
# this key leaks, anyone can publish updates your testers' phones will accept.
# If it is LOST, your 40 testers must uninstall and reinstall (losing local data)
# and you can never update the app they have.
keystore/
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Node / Capacitor.
# package-lock.json IS committed on purpose: the exact plugin versions matter
# here (several nearby packages are archived, paid, or lack a release for this
# Capacitor major), so a reproducible install is worth more than a clean diff.
node_modules/

# Gradle / Android build output
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/build/
android/local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
